An ERA5 file (ECMWF's reanalysis of past weather, on pressure levels, netCDF) read at a site and time

Usage: hpr weather era5 [OPTIONS] --latitude <DEG> --longitude <DEG> --time <TIME> <FILE>

Arguments:
  <FILE>
          The ERA5 pressure-level file, netCDF classic, from the Copernicus Climate Data Store

Options:
      --json
          Print one JSON document on standard output instead of text, errors included

      --latitude <DEG>
          The site's latitude, degrees north (south is negative)

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use color. With auto, output to a terminal is colored, and NO_COLOR, FORCE_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE are followed. JSON output never has color
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --longitude <DEG>
          The site's longitude, degrees east (west is negative)

      --time <TIME>
          The launch time in UTC, such as 2020-02-22T13:00Z

  -o, --output <FILE>
          Write the profile to this file, as JSON

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  Read an ERA5 file at a site and time:
      hpr weather era5 era5.nc --latitude 40.865 --longitude -119.063 --time 2020-02-22T13:00Z
  Save the profile for `hpr sim`:
      hpr weather era5 era5.nc --latitude 40.865 --longitude -119.063 --time 2020-02-22T13:00Z -o profile.json

Guide: https://hpr.fusionspace.co/cli.html#hpr-weather
